{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1484306-experiences-with-cg-magic-styles-or-focus-paradigm-practice-instrument-2e","id":1484306,"title":"Experiences with CG Magic Styles, or Focus (Paradigm, Practice, Instrument) 2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-17T16:09:37-07:00","id":1484306,"title":"Experiences with CG Magic Styles, or Focus (Paradigm, Practice, Instrument) 2e","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> Exactly what says in the tile. <br /> <br /> I'm really excited for Mage: The Ascension Victorian Age, but after reading Mage 20... I really have a lot of problem with the <i>system</i> and <i>some</i> of the cosmology. But I really like the idea of Focus as a mixture of Paradigm, Practice and Instrument in opposition to the totally freeform way of Awakening.<br /> <br /> Travelling here and there I read about magic styles and they are somewhat functional for what I see, but I want to know experiences and other solutions on 2E.<br /> <br /> Other, more simple idea, is give Techn\u00e9 as a free merit to all mages, something not so interesting on my opinion.<br /> <br /> Thanks for reading!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27384-altidiya","name":"altidiya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T01:18:39-07:00","id":1484338,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve barely glanced at Ascension, so I\u2019m not entirely sure what you\u2019re looking for, but in the direction of expanded and more specific foci, have you looked into Magical Traditions? It\u2019s a 1E book, but most of it should still be applicable, and it may at the very least provide ideas to convert.<br /> <br /> Since doing a bit more work with Legacies, they seem like they touch on that idea of Paradigm (and Instrument) a good deal as well. When I started getting into mage, I found them really intimidating, but it\u2019s a lot easier to build them than I thought, and I now feel they\u2019d be almost ubiquitous as a personalized path to enlightenment. <br /> <br /> There\u2019s probably also room to adjust Paradox and requiring Yantras, particularly those relating to a specific occult tradition. Something like there being extra reach depending on how well the yantras embody a particular tradition.<br /> <br /> The problem I\u2019ve run into when trying to make yantras a bigger part of casting has been the table experience (for the players). It\u2019s hard for me to conceptualize, as a storyteller, how to make them relevant constrictions on a story without being a \u201cgotcha\u201d jerk. Most of the time, a mage having appropriate tools seems like it should be a given. It\u2019s rarely an obstacle to get relevant symbolic tools; obviously something rare or expensive (to actually get a substantial bonus) might require some forethought, a skill challenge, maybe even a minor quest. But common components? If a players not really into researching the occult, or struggles with improving those details, I\u2019d expect them to try handwaving it. \u201cI carry a bag of common symbolic tools.\u201d Which is basically what D&amp;D 5E does.<br /> So, I personally struggle with finding the narrative drama, but I would also like to see them become more relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T03:58:11-07:00","id":1484346,"title":"","content":"I've used the M20 system in Awakening. I just made the various instruments work as yantra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Travelling here and there I read about magic styles and they are somewhat functional for what I see, but I want to know experiences and other solutions on 2E. </div> </div> </div>Magic styles (I'm assuming you mean the thing from <i>Chronicler's Guide</i>?) are in my experience quite constraining. Like, you use one style, and only one style; there's not a lot of room for flexibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T10:26:58-07:00","id":1484371,"title":"","content":"The Ascension system is focused on building an entire Paradigm of reality, exploring its implications and limits to determine how a spell is cast, which become less constraining as Arete increases.<br /> <br /> Awakening allows for a lot more flexibility creating spells, since mages have an intuitive understanding of Imagos. Its when they want to make a very powerful spell that they start delving into similar waters. Analyzing symbolism and searching for proper equipment, locating rare ingredients for that one mighty cast or trading for the components, studying a summon so extensively that you know what to expect and saturating an area with enough symbolic trappings that it makes bringing them into reality much easier. A skilled Awakened is likely to behave closer to a Paradigm using mage.<br /> <br /> But a middle ground could probably utilize some ideas from Scars in Deviant. They could tie Arcana dots to the Scars, which would represent the cost of using Lovecraftian superpowers. Paradox would then cause Instability, depending on how many Paradox Reaches are available. <br /> <br /> In this way, mages advancing would mean coming closer to becoming eldritch gods, with the Abyss representing the extreme purposeless chaos of Azathoth and the Supernal being the amoral aid of Hastur. In this sense, yantras would make it easier for mages to focus their abilities to fit into this reality more neatly. In this way, since the consequences of making your powers unstable is increased, theoretically there would be a bigger focus in using yantras to increase spell factors.<br /> <br /> But its just an untested idea, one which would require some time to calibrate mechanically and adjust the lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-18-2022, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T09:00:41-07:00","id":1484424,"title":"","content":"It seems to me it can be made a straightforward matter of &quot;people define their paradigm and then can only use Yantras that incorporate it&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'd think about an addition of being able to <i>only</i> cast like that, but... there's so little you can manage without Yantras anyway.<br /> <br /> Ritual is just... Awakening already has ritual casting without proscription of what they look like, can one not just have players stick to what expresses paradigm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T10:46:27-07:00","id":1484432,"title":"","content":"My personal answer would probably be to grab the Mage Translation Guide and port what you like over to Ascension. It may be designed for First Edition, but it covers enough of the same principles that it won't take too much to adjust for the edition shift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}